  { q: 'Is the exemption available if I buy the new house before selling the old one?', a: 'Yes. The new house may be bought within one year before the date of transfer of the old house, or within two years after it. A house bought earlier than one year before the transfer does not qualify. Keep the purchase deed and the sale deed together to show the dates.' },
  { q: 'Does the exemption cover the whole sale consideration or only the gain?', a: 'Only the long-term capital gain needs to be invested, not the whole sale consideration. If the cost of the new house is equal to or more than the gain, the gain is not charged. If the cost is lower, the shortfall is taxed as capital gain for the year of sale.' },
